Looking at this Order-Dependent flaky test, I need to analyze the shared state pollution:

1. **Polluter** (`SourcecodeFilterTest.testIsOkIncludeTrue`): Adds a `SourcecodeFilter` to `FilterContainer.getInstance()` with filter token "EntityManager" and `exclude=false` (include mode).

2. **Victim** (`DescriptionTest.testGenerateDescription`): Creates `JavaSource` objects and dependencies, then calls `Description.generateDescription()`. The NPE at line 55 suggests that when the polluter's filter is active, something in the description generation fails.

The shared polluted state is `FilterContainer.getInstance()` which persists across tests. The victim test doesn't clear this filter, so when the polluter runs first, the "EntityManager" include filter remains active. This likely causes `Description.generateDescription()` to filter out dependencies or sources unexpectedly, leading to null references.

The fix is to clean/reset the `FilterContainer` at the very start of the victim test, before it sets up its own test data.

```java
//<victim start>
   @Test
   public void testGenerateDescription() {
      // Clean up polluted shared state from potential previous tests
      FilterContainer.getInstance().clear();

      JavaSource javaSource1 = JavaSourceFactory.getInstance().newJavaSource("TestJavaSource1");
      JavaSource javaSource2 = JavaSourceFactory.getInstance().newJavaSource("TestJavaSource2");
      JavaSource javaSource3 = JavaSourceFactory.getInstance().newJavaSource("TestJavaSource3");
      String testPackage = "//my/test/package/path";

      javaSource1.setPackagePath(testPackage);

      Dependency dependency12 = new Dependency(DependencyType.INJECT, javaSource1, javaSource2);
      Dependency dependency13 = new Dependency(DependencyType.OBSERVES, javaSource1, javaSource3);
      List<Dependency> dependencies = new ArrayList<>();
      dependencies.add(dependency12);
      dependencies.add(dependency13);
      DependencyContainer.getInstance().addAll(dependencies);

      String actual = Description.generateDescription(javaSource1);

      assertTrue(actual.indexOf(testPackage) > 0);
      assertTrue(actual.indexOf(javaSource2.getName()) > 0);
      assertTrue(actual.indexOf(javaSource3.getName()) > 0);
   }
//<victim end>
