Looking at this flaky test, I can see the issue: the test expects fields in a specific order (`typeIsSelf` first, then `otherType`), but reflection via `getDeclaredFields()` returns fields in non-deterministic order.

The error shows:
- Expected: `[typeIsSelf=...,otherType=The Other Type]`
- Actual: `[otherType=The Other Type,typeIsSelf=...]`

The test uses reflection to build the string representation, and field iteration order is not guaranteed. I need to make the assertion order-insensitive while preserving the complete structural check.

Since this is a string representation of an object with key-value pairs, I'll parse both expected and actual into a map-like structure and compare them in an order-independent way.

//<fix start>
    @Test
    public void testSelfInstanceTwoVarsReflectionObjectCycle() {
        final SelfInstanceTwoVarsReflectionTestFixture test = new SelfInstanceTwoVarsReflectionTestFixture();
        final String actual = test.toString();
        final String expected = this.toBaseString(test) + "[typeIsSelf=" + this.toBaseString(test) + ",otherType=" + test.getOtherType().toString() + "]";

        // Parse the object representation to compare fields in order-independent manner
        // Format: ClassName@hash[field1=value1,field2=value2]
        final Map<String, String> expectedFields = parseToStringFields(expected);
        final Map<String, String> actualFields = parseToStringFields(actual);

        assertEquals(expectedFields, actualFields);
    }

    private Map<String, String> parseToStringFields(final String toString) {
        final int bracketStart = toString.indexOf('[');
        final int bracketEnd = toString.lastIndexOf(']');
        if (bracketStart == -1 || bracketEnd == -1 || bracketStart >= bracketEnd) {
            return java.util.Collections.emptyMap();
        }
        final String content = toString.substring(bracketStart + 1, bracketEnd);
        final Map<String, String> fields = new java.util.HashMap<>();

        // Simple parser for key=value pairs, handling nested objects
        int depth = 0;
        int start = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < content.length(); i++) {
            final char c = content.charAt(i);
            if (c == '[' || c == '(' || c == '{') {
                depth++;
            } else if (c == ']' || c == ')' || c == '}') {
                depth--;
            } else if (c == ',' && depth == 0) {
                // Found a top-level comma
                final String pair = content.substring(start, i);
                final int eq = pair.indexOf('=');
                if (eq > 0) {
                    fields.put(pair.substring(0, eq), pair.substring(eq + 1));
                }
                start = i + 1;
            }
        }
        // Last pair
        final String pair = content.substring(start);
        final int eq = pair.indexOf('=');
        if (eq > 0) {
            fields.put(pair.substring(0, eq), pair.substring(eq + 1));
        }
        return fields;
    }
//<fix end>

