Looking at this flaky test, I need to analyze the root cause. The error shows that the order of `wsdl:message` elements is non-deterministic - sometimes `GetOrderRequest` comes before `GetOrderResponse`, and sometimes it's the opposite.

The issue is in `CommonsXsdSchemaCollection` which likely uses `HashMap` or similar unordered collections internally when processing XSD imports. When `schemaCollection.setInline(true)` is used, it inlines schemas and the order of generated WSDL message elements becomes non-deterministic.

The test compares XML documents using `assertXMLEqual`, which is order-sensitive for sibling elements. The fix needs to make the comparison order-insensitive while preserving the complete structural check.

Since this is XML comparison, I need to:
1. Parse both documents
2. Sort the message elements deterministically before comparison, OR
3. Use a custom comparison that ignores order of sibling elements with the same name

Looking at the XMLUnit library, I can use `XMLUnit.setIgnoreWhitespace(true)` which is already set, but I need to also handle element order. However, XMLUnit's `assertXMLEqual` by default checks order.

The best approach is to normalize both documents by sorting `wsdl:message` elements before comparison. I'll need to implement a helper that sorts sibling elements with the same tag name.

Actually, looking more carefully at XMLUnit, I can use `Diff` with custom `ElementQualifier` or use `DetailedDiff` with specific options. But the simplest robust fix is to sort the message elements in both documents before comparison.

Let me implement a solution that sorts the `wsdl:message` elements by their `name` attribute before comparison:

//<fix start>
	@Test
	public void testImport() throws Exception {
		ClassPathResource resource = new ClassPathResource("importing.xsd", getClass());
		CommonsXsdSchemaCollection schemaCollection = new CommonsXsdSchemaCollection(resource);
		schemaCollection.setInline(true);
		schemaCollection.afterPropertiesSet();
		definition.setSchemaCollection(schemaCollection);

		definition.setPortTypeName("Order");
		definition.setTargetNamespace("http://www.springframework.org/spring-ws/import/definitions");
		definition.setLocationUri("http://localhost:8080/");
		definition.afterPropertiesSet();

		DOMResult domResult = new DOMResult();
		transformer.transform(definition.getSource(), domResult);

		Document result = (Document) domResult.getNode();
		Document expected = documentBuilder.parse(getClass().getResourceAsStream("import-inline.wsdl"));

		// Sort wsdl:message elements by name attribute to ensure deterministic order
		sortMessageElements(result);
		sortMessageElements(expected);

		assertXMLEqual("Invalid WSDL built", expected, result);
	}

	private void sortMessageElements(Document document) {
		org.w3c.dom.Element root = document.getDocumentElement();
		org.w3c.dom.NodeList messageNodes = root.getElementsByTagNameNS("http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/wsdl/", "message");

		// Collect message elements and their names
		java.util.List<org.w3c.dom.Element> messages = new java.util.ArrayList<>();
		for (int i = 0; i < messageNodes.getLength(); i++) {
			messages.add((org.w3c.dom.Element) messageNodes.item(i));
		}

		// Sort by name attribute
		messages.sort((e1, e2) -> {
			String name1 = e1.getAttribute("name");
			String name2 = e2.getAttribute("name");
			return name1.compareTo(name2);
		});

		// Remove and re-append in sorted order
		for (org.w3c.dom.Element message : messages) {
			root.removeChild(message);
		}
		for (org.w3c.dom.Element message : messages) {
			root.appendChild(message);
		}
	}
//<fix end>

