Looking at this flaky test, I need to analyze what's causing the non-deterministic behavior.

The test creates an `ImmutableMap` with two entries:
```java
Map<String, Long> notificationsMap =
    ImmutableMap.of(someNamespace, someNotificationId, anotherNamespace, anotherNotificationId);
```

The issue is that when this map is serialized to JSON in the `assembleLongPollRefreshUrl` method, the iteration order of the map entries can vary. While `ImmutableMap.of()` with 2 entries does preserve insertion order, the actual serialization in the production code likely uses a `HashMap` or similar unordered structure internally, or the JSON serialization itself doesn't guarantee order.

The test assertion checks for a specific JSON string with a fixed order:
```
[{"namespaceName":"someName","notificationId":1},{"namespaceName":"anotherName","notificationId":2}]
```

But if the map iteration order changes, the JSON could be:
```
[{"namespaceName":"anotherName","notificationId":2},{"namespaceName":"someName","notificationId":1}]
```

To fix this ID flaky test, I need to parse both the expected and actual JSON and compare them in an order-insensitive way while preserving all assertions. I'll use Jackson's `JsonNode` for tree comparison, which handles array order properly when we sort or compare as sets.

Let me check what imports are available and what I need to add. The test already has access to various utilities. I'll need to add Jackson imports for JSON parsing.

Here's the fix:

//<fix start>
  @Test
  public void testAssembleLongPollRefreshUrlWithMultipleNamespaces() throws Exception {
    String someUri = someServerUrl;
    String someAppId = "someAppId";
    String someCluster = "someCluster+ &.-_someSign";
    String someNamespace = "someName";
    String anotherNamespace = "anotherName";
    long someNotificationId = 1;
    long anotherNotificationId = 2;
    Map<String, Long> notificationsMap =
        ImmutableMap.of(someNamespace, someNotificationId, anotherNamespace, anotherNotificationId);

    String longPollRefreshUrl =
        remoteConfigLongPollService
            .assembleLongPollRefreshUrl(someUri, someAppId, someCluster, null, notificationsMap);

    assertTrue(longPollRefreshUrl.contains(someServerUrl + "/notifications/v2?"));
    assertTrue(longPollRefreshUrl.contains("appId=" + someAppId));
    assertTrue(longPollRefreshUrl.contains("cluster=someCluster%2B+%26.-_someSign"));

    // Extract and decode the notifications parameter from the URL
    String notificationsParam = null;
    java.net.URI uri = java.net.URI.create(longPollRefreshUrl);
    String query = uri.getQuery();
    for (String param : query.split("&")) {
      if (param.startsWith("notifications=")) {
        notificationsParam = java.net.URLDecoder.decode(param.substring("notifications=".length()), "UTF-8");
        break;
      }
    }
    assertNotNull("notifications parameter should be present", notificationsParam);

    // Parse actual JSON and expected JSON, then compare as sets (order-insensitive)
    com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.ObjectMapper mapper = new com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.ObjectMapper();
    com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.JsonNode actualNotifications = mapper.readTree(notificationsParam);

    // Build expected notifications array (order doesn't matter)
    java.util.Set<com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.JsonNode> expectedNotifications = new java.util.HashSet<>();
    expectedNotifications.add(mapper.createObjectNode()
        .put("namespaceName", someNamespace)
        .put("notificationId", someNotificationId));
    expectedNotifications.add(mapper.createObjectNode()
        .put("namespaceName", anotherNamespace)
        .put("notificationId", anotherNotificationId));

    // Compare as sets - order insensitive but complete
    assertTrue("notifications should contain exactly the expected entries",
        actualNotifications.isArray() && actualNotifications.size() == 2);
    java.util.Set<com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.JsonNode> actualSet = new java.util.HashSet<>();
    for (com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.JsonNode node : actualNotifications) {
      actualSet.add(node);
    }
    assertEquals(expectedNotifications, actualSet);
  }
//<fix end>

